# Method 3 — Key Event titles, biological levels and full description text.
#
# Endpoint : https://aopwiki.rdf.bigcat-bioinformatics.org/sparql/
# Release  : AOPWikiRDF @ 97191db, data generated 2026-08-01  (see pinned-release.yaml)
# Used by  : analysis/method3/m3_01_snapshot.py  ->  data/method3/corpus/ke_descriptions.csv
#
# This is `method1c_ke_inventory.rq` with the description TEXT projected instead of its length.
# Method 1 needed the length, because it measures how description availability predicts gene
# recovery. Method 3 needs the text: the adjudicating curator reads the KE description to
# decide whether a ranked pathway actually captures the mechanism the KE names, and the
# evidence packets have to be self-contained so the adjudication makes no network calls.
#
# The descriptions are the reason to take this from the pinned release rather than from the
# builder's own /get_ke_options. The builder serves a snapshot of 1561 KEs against the pin's
# 1595 (upstream issue #239), so ~34 KEs — including several in these three networks — would
# otherwise arrive with no description at all, and a KE with no description is exactly the one
# an adjudicator is most likely to get wrong.
#
# `dc:description` and the biological level are both OPTIONAL. Rows are returned for KEs that
# have neither, so this doubles as the check on how much of each organ network is describable:
# brain 118 of 203, kidney 20 of 68, lung 77 of 134 carry a description.
#
# The biological level uses NCI Thesaurus C25664 and takes Molecular / Cellular / Tissue /
# Organ / Individual / Population. It decides the +1.0 confidence bonus, which was
# tier-deciding for 84 % of the liver campaign's KEs — so an unbound biolevel is not a cosmetic
# gap, it silently costs a point.

PREFIX aopo: <http://aopkb.org/aop_ontology#>
PREFIX dc:   <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/>
PREFIX nci:  <http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT DISTINCT ?keid ?ke ?ketitle ?biolevel ?description
WHERE {
  ?ke a aopo:KeyEvent ;
      rdfs:label ?keid ;
      dc:title   ?ketitle .
  OPTIONAL { ?ke nci:C25664 ?biolevel }
  OPTIONAL { ?ke dc:description ?description }
}
